DVDdb, a php+MySQL DVD Database.


What is it?
-----------

This system was designed to allow friends to keep track of what DVD's
they owned, and what was on loan to other people.

How is it available?
--------------------

DVDdb is available under the terms of the GPL.

Where is it available?
----------------------

You can download the DVDdb code from http://globalmegacorp.org/dvddb (You
can also see a demonstration version of it running there).


How do I install it?
--------------------

See the INSTALL file, located in the same directory as this file.
(A basic level of MySQL, PHP and *nix knowledge is assumed).


How do I upgrade from a previous version?
-----------------------------------------
See the UPGRADE file for information about upgrading from earlier
versions.


What's new in this version?
---------------------------
See the Changelog file to see what's new in this version.


Who's responsible for this?
-----------------------------

DVDdb is written by James Gurney (james@globalmegacorp.org)
Region code and design suggestions from John Gross (grossy@midnite.net.au)


What can I do for you?
----------------------

Drop me a line and let me know you're using it, and if you like it. If you
don't like it, don't use it. If you'd like to suggest enhancements, let me
know. If you'd like to contribute enhancements, let me know. If you find
bugs, badly written code, inefficient code, or downright silly code, let
me know! Thanks!


What does the future look like?
-------------------------------

See the TODO file for a list of things currently planned for addition.


More questions?
---------------

See the rather poor FAQ I put together at
http://globalmegacorp.org/dvddb/faq.php or just drop me an email.


